Landed as Gerrit change 1604 (commit 538cc38e93), MERGED with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, 0 unresolved comments.

Delivered tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_cloud_unassign_6a74.py (4 tests, test-only; git show --stat confirms 1 file changed, nothing under src/):
- both empty sentinels ("" and None) PUT Cloud's {"accountId": null} to /rest/api/3/issue/<key>/assignee and spawn no ACLI subprocess;
- the co-submit case fires the unassign AND emits a workitem edit argv carrying --summary with no --assignee flag;
- a non-empty assignee still takes the validate-then-edit path, normalised to the matched accountId.

Following the DC sibling's rigor the oracle is positive about absence: it captures the REAL REST request production unassign_issue builds rather than settling for a stubbed method call. Falsifiability checked: reverting AcliClient.update_issue to the pre-85a1 verbatim-forward behavior makes all 4 tests FAIL; restored and all 4 pass. make lint and make typecheck pass from the worktree venv.
